{"name":"Paper Moon","hex":"#ead4a6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"paper","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sheet material typically used for writing on or printing on (or as a non-waterproof container), usually made by draining cellulose fibres from a suspension in water.","Ellipsis of newspaper; anything used as such (such as a newsletter or listing magazine)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of paper.","Insubstantial (from the weakness of common paper)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paper"},{"term":"moon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Moon (“the Earth's only permanent natural satellite”)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any natural satellite of a planet.","The light received from the Moon; moonlight."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Paper Moon (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Paper Moon is a 1973 American road comedy-drama film directed by Peter Bogdanovich and released by Paramount Pictures. Screenwriter Alvin Sargent adapted the script from the 1971 novel Addie Pray by Joe David Brown. The film, shot in black-and-white, is set in Kansas and Missouri during the Great Depression. It stars the real-life father and daughter pairing of Ryan and Tatum O'Neal as protagonists Moze and Addie."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/71/Paper-moon_small.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paper_Moon_(film)","wikidata":"Q603162"},{"title":"Paper Moon (American TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Paper Moon is an American sitcom which aired for one season on ABC in 1974. The series starred Christopher Connelly and Jodie Foster."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/8a/Paper_Moon_TV_series_title_card.PNG/330px-Paper_Moon_TV_series_title_card.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paper_Moon_(American_TV_series)","wikidata":"Q115821668"},{"title":"Paper","blocks":[{"text":"Paper is a thin sheet of matted cellulose fibers. Largely derived from lignocellulose, paper is created from a pulp dissolved into a slurry that is drained and dried into sheets. Different types of paper are defined by constituent fiber, paper pulp, sizing, coating, paper size, paper density and grammage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Various_products_made_from_paper.JPG/330px-Various_products_made_from_paper.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paper","wikidata":"Q11472"},{"title":"Moon","blocks":[{"text":"The Moon is the only natural satellite of Earth. It orbits Earth in an elliptical path, at a distance that varies over the year, averaging around 378,000 kilometers (235,000 mi). It completes an orbit in relation to Earth and the Sun (synodically) every 29.5 days. The Moon and Earth are bound by gravitational attraction, which is stronger on the sides facing each other. The resulting tidal forces are the main driver of Earth's tides, and have pulled the Moon to always face Earth with the same near side. This tidal locking effectively synchronizes the Moon's rotation period to its orbital period."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/FullMoon2010.jpg/330px-FullMoon2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moon","wikidata":"Q405"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Tatum_O%27Neal_Oscar_1974_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Tatum_O%27Neal_Oscar_1974_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Tatum_O%27Neal_Oscar_1974_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Tatum_O%27Neal_Oscar_1974_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Tatum_O%27Neal_Oscar_1974_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Tatum_O%27Neal_Oscar_1974_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tatum O'Neal in 1974, winning the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actress for Paper Moon","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATatum_O'Neal_Oscar_1974_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Paper_Moon_television_1974.JPG/500px-Paper_Moon_television_1974.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Paper_Moon_television_1974.JPG/500px-Paper_Moon_television_1974.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APaper_Moon_television_1974.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Paper_Moon_TV_series_Foster_Connelly_1974.jpg/500px-Paper_Moon_TV_series_Foster_Connelly_1974.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Paper_Moon_TV_series_Foster_Connelly_1974.jpg/500px-Paper_Moon_TV_series_Foster_Connelly_1974.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APaper_Moon_TV_series_Foster_Connelly_1974.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Chinese_hemp_paper_western_han.jpg/500px-Chinese_hemp_paper_western_han.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Chinese_hemp_paper_western_han.jpg/500px-Chinese_hemp_paper_western_han.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=